  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), three-quarter view from the pilot's left rear, front of the stick (trigger) to the left, left side of the grip and the GNX EVO base control panel (pilot side) visible, right side of the grip hidden",
  "mappingSource": "MobiFlight device definition vkbsim_gladiator_evo_f14.joystick.json (https://github.com/MobiFlight/MobiFlight-Connector/blob/main/src/MobiFlightConnector/Joysticks/vkbsim/vkbsim_gladiator_evo_f14.joystick.json, community, labels Trigger Soft/Hard, Red Button, Weapon Select Push/SP PH/SW/Gun/Off, Side Button, Paddle Switch, Pinky Switch, Hat, En1, Sw1, F1-F3) as cited by the catalog; VKB publishes no binding template for the F-14 grip (vkbsimcontrollers.com/pages/downloads); base labels F1/F2/F3, Sw1, En1 are printed on the base",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "The four weapon-select positions (SP/PH, SW, GUN, OFF) are positions of one rotary drum (ribbed ring with red index mark at the left of the grip head; labels readable on gallery-2); they are stacked on the drum here. The push (BTN4) is assumed to be pressing the drum's large end cap (\"Four-Stage Ammo Selector with Safety Lock and Push Button\", VKB product page) - position medium. \"Side button\" = the white button on the plate on the left side of the grip (the only side button); the white ribbed thumb wheel just above that plate is most likely the DLC axis (product page: \"1x DLC Axis\"), which the catalog does not list - not marked. The twist adapter (Z axis, lockable) is not in the catalog either. Pinky switch (BTN7) is not visible here: a small round button on the right side of the grip just above the paddle (visible on gallery-4 at about 0.62 0.47) is the likely pinky switch. the centre base wheel (with the grey tab, between Sw1 and En1) is the base throttle/axis wheel - not a catalog part, not marked. catalog discrepancy: base buttons 1-3 list JOY_BTN21-23 AND JOY_BTN27-29; the MobiFlight F-14 map has F1-F3 = 21-23 and only 24 buttons in total (no 27-29).",
